            <ArticleTitle>[Adalat effects on clinical course of coronary heart disease, peripheral circulation and myocardial perfusion in patients with stenosing coronary atherosclerosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>61-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To study adalate effects on the clinical picture, systemic microcirculation and myocardial blood flow in postmyocardial infarction patients.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIALS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Adalate was given for two weeks in a daily dose 30 mg to 17 patients with angina of effort who had survived macrofocal myocardial infarction. The examination was made with tetrapolar chest rheography, polarography, biomicroscopy, computed tomography.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Positive clinical changes were seen in 92% of the treated patients: the need in nitroglycerine reduced 1.8 times, muscular performance rose by 24%, skin O2 tension increased by 37.5%, central hemodynamics, microcirculation and myocardial blood flow improved noticeably.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Adalate has a good antianginal and antiischemic action due to positive hemodynamic effects.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
